{"id": "wikibooks:jerk-grilled-salmon", "verdict": "keep", "recipes": [{"source": "https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3AJerk_Grilled_Salmon", "status": "fixed", "reason": "Move the oil-soaked grill towel out of ingredients and clarify that it is equipment, not part of the marinade.", "ingredients": ["4 ea. (24 ounces) salmon fillets, skin on one side", "2 tbsp minced ginger", "2 Scotch bonnet or habanero peppers, stemmed and optionally seeded", "1½ tsp salt", "1½ tsp freshly ground black pepper", "¼ tsp freshly ground grains of paradise, or more pepper", "½ tsp freshly ground allspice", "½ tsp freshly ground cinnamon", "¼ tsp freshly grated nutmeg", "8 sprigs thyme", "½ cup olive oil"], "steps": ["Purée ginger, peppers, salt, black pepper, grains of paradise, allspice, cinnamon, nutmeg and thyme in a blender or food processor until smooth. Slowly drizzle in oil with the machine running.", "Pour into a gallon-size zip-top bag, add salmon and refrigerate at least 10 minutes.", "Heat about 28 charcoal briquets in a large chimney starter and disperse evenly around the grill bottom.", "Replace the grate and quickly grease it using a heat-resistant towel tied with twine and soaked in oil.", "Add salmon skin-side down and cook covered, turning often, until pink throughout and easily flaked with a fork.", "Transfer to a plate, cover with aluminum foil and rest 5–7 minutes before serving warm."]}]}
